		<gameEnder />
		<letterStack>
			<letters>
				<li Class="StandardLetter">
					<def>BadNonUrgent</def>
					<label>Cold snap</label>
					<disappearAtTick>-1</disappearAtTick>
					<text>An unusual cold snap has set in.

Cold snaps can quickly kill by hypothermia. Be sure to build a heated space to survive, wear appropriate apparel, and try to harvest crops before they freeze and die.</text>
				</li>
				<li Class="StandardLetter">
					<def>BadNonUrgent</def>
					<label>Psychic drone</label>
					<disappearAtTick>-1</disappearAtTick>
					<text>Every colonist of the male gender winces in pain!

Some distant engine of hatred is stirring. It is projecting a powerful psychic drone over this entire region, on a frequency that only seems to affect the male gender. For a few days, some people's mood will be quite a bit worse.</text>
				</li>
				<li Class="StandardLetter">
					<def>BadNonUrgent</def>
					<label>Breakdown: battery</label>
					<lookTarget>Thing_Battery92084</lookTarget>
					<disappearAtTick>-1</disappearAtTick>
					<text>One of your machines (battery) has broken down. It won't work until a colonist with the Construction work type goes and fixes it.</text>
				</li>
				<li Class="StandardLetter">
					<def>BadNonUrgent</def>
					<label>Solar flare</label>
					<disappearAtTick>-1</disappearAtTick>
					<text>A solar flare has begun.

The intense radiation will shut down all electrical devices.

It should pass in about a day.</text>
				</li>
				<li Class="StandardLetter">
					<def>Good</def>
					<label>Bandit camp opportunity</label>
					<lookTarget>@WorldObject_94</lookTarget>
					<disappearAtTick>-1</disappearAtTick>
					<text>Onesan, prime councilor of Wastedveler, has sent us a message.

Apparently bandits based in a nearby camp have been raiding their caravans. They've asked us to destroy it, which means eliminating all enemies and turrets.

If we succeed, their relations will improve, and they'll send us this reward:

Megascreen television</text>
				</li>
				<li Class="StandardLetter">
					<def>Good</def>
					<label>Item stash opportunity</label>
					<lookTarget>@WorldObject_95</lookTarget>
					<disappearAtTick>-1</disappearAtTick>
					<text>Maker, prime councilor of Veeveussia Confederation, has sent us a message.

They've learned that a collection of valuable items have been left for the taking not far from us. The collection consists of:

  Fennec foxskin tribalwear (poor)
  Cloth Jedi garb (poor)
  Cloth Jedi garb (poor)
  Cloth tribalwear (good)
  Cloth Jedi garb (normal)
  Cloth Jedi garb (normal)
  Timber wolfskin parka (good)
  Catskin parka (superior)
  Synthread parka (good)

Unfortunately, it won’t last - others will take the items in 27 days if we don't.

Valuables tend to attract danger, so beware.

Maker says that there is an enemy outpost nearby.</text>
				</li>
				<li Class="StandardLetter">
					<def>Good</def>
					<label>New lovers</label>
					<lookTarget>Thing_Human1785</lookTarget>
					<disappearAtTick>-1</disappearAtTick>
					<text>Trev and Kimmy have come together and are now lovers.</text>
				</li>
				<li Class="StandardLetter">
					<def>BadNonUrgent</def>
					<label>Breakdown: electric stove</label>
					<lookTarget>Thing_ElectricStove91699</lookTarget>
					<disappearAtTick>-1</disappearAtTick>
					<text>One of your machines (electric stove) has broken down. It won't work until a colonist with the Construction work type goes and fixes it.</text>
				</li>
				<li Class="StandardLetter">
					<def>BadUrgent</def>
					<label>Raid</label>
					<lookTarget>Thing_Human405953</lookTarget>
					<disappearAtTick>-1</disappearAtTick>
					<text>A group of tribespeople from Coalition of Beboa have arrived nearby.

They will prepare for a while, then attack.

Prepare a defense or attack them pre-emptively.</text>
				</li>
			</letters>
		</letterStack>
